
  [38;5;153mroutes/users.js:6[39m is the only occurrence. The rename itself is one line. The consequence is not:

  - [38;5;153mREADME.md[39m states field names in [38;5;153mGET /users[39m are part of the contract, and [1mchanges go through a versioned endpoint[0m.
  - Named consumers: the web app, the iOS app (3.2 and later), and the nightly partner export. Shipped iOS builds can't
    be updated in lockstep, so a straight rename breaks them until users upgrade.

  "For consistency with the other endpoints" is a real motivation — [38;5;153m/orders[39m already returns [38;5;153muser_id[39m — but it doesn't by
  itself resolve the compatibility question.

